Rule 1 (number of threads returned is positive)
{v_1 : int} |= v_1 ≥ 1
>>
Rule 2 (number of threads returned is not zero)
{v_1 : int} |= v_1 ≠ 0
>>
Rule 4 (adding one increases the returned thread count)
{v_1 : int} |= v_1 + 1 > v_1
>>
Rule 5 (valid non-negative loop range derived from returned thread count)
{v_1 : int} |= v_1 ≥ 1 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_1 - 1] : i ≥ 0
>>
Rule 6 (if more than one thread, at least two; otherwise exactly one)
{v_1 : int} |= if v_1 ≥ 2 then v_1 - 1 ≥ 1 else v_1 = 1
>>
Rule 7 (returned value is an integer multiple of 1)
{v_1 : int} |= v_1 % 1 = 0
